ed commands use platform conventions.\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx861B3G_ -> explicit release contracts and corpus-derived non-vacuity -> unchanged 50-percent reduction threshold documented with framing/receipt regeneration; corpus-derived question/harness counts and adversarial receipt checks; all documented CLI and SDK installs initialize a tracker before package use plus live ten-question packet proof.\nPRRT_kwDOVlkMx861B3HC -> use the platform shell for linked commands -> default-shell execution replaces the POSIX-only launcher, with baseline before each proof; harness PATH composition and linked commands use platform conventions.\n\nShared-class closure also includes dotted home aliases with an index loop (including long punctuation), WSL/UNC and resolved home roots, unchanged stored-state read compatibility, complete production/acquisition member/optional/dynamic import guards, and real README CLI/SDK initialization. The added directory-host lifecycle catches relative-root drift and raw core-settings reads using an explicit non-default extension section, with five independent source reverts. Packed SDK consumers exercise relative roots. No finding was refused. Review threads remain untouched for the orchestrator; no merge or release."
