  "2026-11-09T01:40:54.555Z",codex-agent,"Review round five (auto) addressed all four remaining non-blocking findings and closed each class. 1) Linked release-gate timeouts: both npm and bun release:check entries moved from 1800 to 5400 seconds, above the measured 2552-second run; a class test now refuses any linked release:check entry at or below 3000 seconds across every tracker toon. Red proof: the class test failed with AssertionError on the pre-fix 1800-second entries and passes after the update. 2) README archive install now creates and enters a fresh sibling consumer directory before installing the archive, so pm init can never provision the source checkout's own tracker; registry wording now says fresh projects outside the checkout; the archive-provenance test accepts parent-relative archive paths and a class test requires every documented archive install to create and enter a fresh consumer directory first. Red proof: the class test failed with AssertionError on the pre-fix package-directory install. 3) The module-load home lookup is guarded: a throwing homedir now degrades to an empty home list while every static private-path rule stays active; this was the only module-load environment lookup in the package. Regression test plus a behavioral revert proof in the disposable harness: reverting the guard makes the focused test fail red with a named assertion (63 red and 63 restored-green proofs in the full acceptance). 4) The public harness now certifies the historical failing run with the structured selectedTestFailed check before the fail receipt row is recorded, keeping the exit-status and regex checks; the class test requires every failing-run receipt row to be preceded by the structured certification and failed with AssertionError before the fix. A full public harness run passed: three passing scoped runs plus the reproduced historical regression, now proven to fail as a named assertion event."
  "2026-11-09T01:42:33.750Z",codex-agent,"Round five complete. Local gates on the fix commit: full linked suite 95 of 95 tests pass (node --test, 2 workers), focused review-class and privacy suites 30 of 30 including the three new class tests and the home-lookup regression, behavioral revert acceptance 63 red and 63 restored-green proofs including the new module-load guard, public harness run passed three scoped runs plus the reproduced historical regression now certified as a named assertion event, typecheck, lint, duplication 0 percent, docstrings 101 of 101, identity gate zero violations, changelog check up to date. A pre-existing local-only tracker-health warning remains: the installed pm-github extension reports a host version skew that also reproduces on the unmodified prior head, so it is host environment state, not a repository defect; CI ran the same gate green. Releasing the claim after the final push."
  "2026-11-09T05:54:57.812Z",codex-agent,"Continuation round six: preserved the existing branch and sparse-array guard hunk, inspected every unresolved thread with complete comments and the latest CodeRabbit review (no outside-diff findings). Four valid findings remain: archive path resolution, sparse-array length before parsing, sha256sum prerequisites, and runtime workflow splitting. Work proceeds in an isolated package worktree; no duplicate item or PR. Regression proofs will use disposable copies and all review threads remain untouched."
  "2026-11-09T05:57:35.728Z",codex-agent,"Round-six implementation: all four findings verified valid. Archive install now captures the source archive path before changing directories and a shell fixture proves the referenced file exists. Sparse arrays above 200000 reject before parser entry and before tracker writes, with boundary/public-data controls. Packed acceptance shares one required-tool inventory with its prerequisite check, including sha256sum. Workflow guards isolate letter/digit/hyphen/underscore jobs and named/unnamed indented steps; the same-class scan also covers Bun full gates and yaml extensions. Five independent behavioral mutations are added to the disposable revert harness. Focused linked gates pass; typecheck, lint, zero duplication and 101 documented declarations pass. The existing full gate measured about 42 minutes previously; run npm first and run Bun locally only if the measured pair fits the approximate 60-minute budget, otherwise require CI for Bun."
  "2026-11-09T06:06:39.026Z",codex-agent,"The first full npm release run passed 98 tests at 100 percent coverage, all static gates and packed acceptance (45 files; 62 commands per npm/Bun manager; exact Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0), then correctly stopped when a new step-parser mutation failed to turn its regression red. This was a deficient adversarial fixture: the unpinned step followed a gate step instead of a pinned setup. Corrected the fixture to place the unpinned setup immediately after a pinned named setup, preserving valid named/unnamed controls. Do not count the initial full run as a pass; retry the final source and all revert proofs."
  "2026-11-09T06:39:48.005Z",codex-agent,"Round six complete: all four unresolved findings are valid and fixed. PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861G2nE: capture the source archive path before changing directories; regression ^documented archive installs. PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861G2nH: bound sparse-array length before traversal, parser entry or native writes; regression ^sparse arrays refuse. PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861G2nN: one shared packed prerequisite/probe inventory includes sha256sum; regression ^packed acceptance requires. PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861G2nP: isolate hyphenated/numbered jobs and named/unnamed indented setup steps; regression ^runtime provisioning isolates. Every new behavioral revert proves baseline exit 0, named assertion failure exit 1 and restored exit 0 in disposable copies; the workflow finding has two independent mutations. No outside-diff findings remain in the latest review. Same-class review also covers Bun gates, both workflow extensions and the captured-path provenance test. Final isolated-home/Git npm run release:check PASSED in 1892.25 seconds: 98/98 tests, zero skips/failures, all 603 statements, 337 branches, 170 functions and 489 lines covered across nine runtime modules at unchanged 100-percent thresholds. Full revert acceptance: 68 red/68 restored-green proofs, 4 linked clean-build proofs, 3 wrong-error-code probes. Packed acceptance: 1/1 journey, 45 allowlisted files, 62 commands per npm/Bun manager, SDK/CLI on exact Node 22.19.0 and 26.13.0 with Git absent; ignored-build mutation and swapped-archive checks pass. Typecheck, lint, zero duplication, 101 documented declarations, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), identity, tracker health, package, changelog and publish-attestation gates pass. Full bun run release:check is deferred to CI: a measured pair exceeds the approximate 60-minute aggregate local budget after the initial fixture correction/retry; this is missing certification, not a pass. Final-head CI remains pending at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/pull/1/checks; the Node 26 job runs the complete Bun gate. Development-only audit risk is separately tracked in pm-case-dev-audit (three moderate entries; package/lockfile unchanged). No pm CLI/SDK bug was encountered. Keep this item in progress for orchestrator verification; leave every review thread untouched."
  "2026-11-09T06:41:54.469Z",codex-agent,"Pushed implementation commit bf3b85d17332582e08f4db916478e90985393339 to the existing feat/case PR. Exact implementation-head CI is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/42574510403 and CodeQL is queued at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/actions/runs/42574510296. Full Bun gate certification remains pending in CI. This final handoff receipt changes tracker metadata only; fresh final-head checks must be inspected after its push at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/pull/1/checks. Queued, pending, skipped and neutral checks do not establish approval. No threads were replied to, resolved or reacted to; no merge or release was performed. The claim stays released and the item stays in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-09T08:24:56.060Z",codex-agent,"Final scoped review round: continuing the existing PR at 0ff5cc2. The branch contains main and the five reported findings are valid. Limit changes to archive certification wording, enforced page-size wording, expected corpus refusal filtering with one behavioral regression, mutation restoration, and the two-case proof precondition. Run focused tests, typecheck, lint and changelog:check only; full gates remain with CI. No review-thread interactions."
  "2026-11-09T08:27:33.399Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861K4Fq behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy, reverted only test/corpus.ts to the pre-fix catch. node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern=\"^corpus guard skips only invalid_input\" test/corpus-privacy.test.ts failed 1/1 with ERR_ASSERTION: Missing expected exception. Restoring the fixed catch passed 1/1. The regression executes the actual passage guard statement and covers accepted input, invalid_input skip, TypeError propagation and outcome_unknown propagation. Pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress passed all 12 focused tests with zero skips. npm run typecheck and npm run lint passed."
  "2026-11-09T08:28:21.739Z",codex-agent,"Final scoped round validation: node test/public-harness.acceptance.ts passed in a disposable package copy using the frozen public repositories: three selected tests pass, one historical regression fails as expected, restored execution passes, and the finally block verifies original file bytes. Generated receipts/logs stayed in the disposable copy. PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861K4Ff now distinguishes acceptance-created and separately created release archives in ARCHITECTURE.md and README.md; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861K4Fl states the enforced 6400 UTF-8 byte bound and ceil(bytes/4) estimate; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861K4Fq filters only invalid_input and has the recorded red/green proof; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861K4Fu protects the initial mutation write and asserts exact restoration in finally; PRRT_kwDOVlkMx861K4Fy asserts at least two planned cases before indexed access. All 12 focused tests, typecheck and lint passed. Only the requested corpus regression was added; no helpers, dependency changes, review-thread interactions or full local gates. Release the claim, regenerate and check the changelog, then push the existing PR branch; CI owns full certification. No new pm CLI/SDK defects were encountered."
  "2026-11-09T09:32:37.065Z","harness:claude-code","Orchestrator fix: branch protection requires the checks 'test (22)' and 'test (26)', but the exact-version matrix (22.19.0, 26.13.0) reported 'test (22.19.0)' and 'test (26.13.0)', so the PR stayed BLOCKED with every check green. The test job is now named 'test (${{ matrix.major }})' with a matrix include of node-version plus major, and runtimeProvisioning accepts that form while still requiring exactly 22=22.19.0 and 26=26.13.0. workflow + review-classes tests 13/13; mutating major 26 to 25 fails 2."
  "2026-11-14T09:59:18.376Z",codex-sweep-1114,"Release-attribution correction: completed_at = 2026-11-09T09:34:31Z from https://github.com/unbraind/pm-case/pull/1 (merge SHA f9abde559d22852b958ad92e3da81787de43d6c0); no fetched release tag contains that merge commit, so release remains unset and this work is genuinely unreleased."
